% expect-output: m
% expect-output: 10.0
% expect-output: 10.0
% expect-output: l
% expect-output: 10.0
% expect-output: 20.0
% expect-output: c
% expect-output: 10.0
% expect-output: 50.0
% expect-output: 40.0
% expect-output: 40.0
% expect-output: 30.0
% expect-output: 30.0
% expect-output: h
% expect-output: 0
% Scenario: pathforall enumerates the current path. Each segment runs
% the procedure of its kind with its coordinates in the user space of
% the CTM in effect, so a path built under a scale reads back in the
% numbers it was built with; the procedures print the kind letter, then
% the coordinates top-down. An empty path runs nothing.
% Expect: m 10 10, l 10 20, c 10 50 40 40 30 30, h, then 0.
2 2 scale
10 10 moveto 20 10 lineto 30 30 40 40 50 10 curveto closepath
{ (m) = = = } { (l) = = = } { (c) = = = = = = = } { (h) = } pathforall
newpath
0 { pop 1 add } dup dup dup pathforall =
